WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.760
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and this week
they finally released the first teaser for

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:10.670
Series 8 so I wanted to do a breakdown of
everything we know about the episodes including

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:11.690
the premiere date. I know in the teaser it
listed August as a general start date but

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:15.410
there's a really good chance they'll show
either the first episode at Comic Con, which

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:19.060
is the last weekend in July. Or they'll
show the first full trailer.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:22.180
If you're finding me for the first time
I'm doing bonus videos for Doctor Who until

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:27.810
it comes back. Be sure to subscribe to get
everything. When it does come back I'll

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.950
be doing weekly episode videos with a giveaway,
Q&amp;As and Bonus videos. Basically the same

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.570
thing I'm doing for Game of Thrones right
now.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.820
There's been a history of showing the first
episode at a convention a week in advance

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.180
of the world premiere, but doing some reverse
math. If you look at the 50th Anniversary,

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.140
they didn't start showing trailers till
about 3 or 4 weeks before the episode. So

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.250
it's possible that if they only show the
trailer at Comic Con, the first episode won't

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.910
premiere till the end of August.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:49.960
If you're confused about why they haven't
already told us the exact day Series 8 will

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.620
premiere, it's not because they're trying
to be mysterious. It's because they're

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.180
not done editing the episodes.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:01.590
In order to start showing episodes they have
to have enough of them completely finished

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.000
so that they can air one a week for the duration
of the series. So right now they're still

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:04.439
shooting the last couple and almost finished
editing the first couple.

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:06.380
I wouldn't be surprised if they were doing
final edits on the last episode after the

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.850
first couple have already aired. TV is a little
weird in that production happens on a rolling

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:11.780
basis, so that different episodes are always
in various states of production at any given

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:12.020
time. Unlike a movie which has to be completely
finished before the premiere.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:14.770
That doesn't even take into account the
Christmas Special. They haven't made a formal

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:17.950
announcement, but there will be 13 episodes
this year. They'll all air this year and

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:22.149
historically series have 12 regular episodes
with 1 Christmas Special. I hope they don't

00:01:22.149 --> 00:01:23.770
wait till Comic Con to make the announcement,
but either way we'll know by July if that

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:27.209
13th episode is the Christmas Special.

00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:32.420
So the good news is, thanks to people taking
pictures and doing detective work around the

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.299
set, we know a lot about what each of the
episodes are going to be this year. Not full

00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:38.420
plots, that would be kind of spoilery, but
we do know a lot of general things. So here's

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.359
a breakdown of everything we know by order
of episode:

00:01:39.359 --> 00:01:43.179
Episodes 1 will be in Victorian London with
the Paternoster Gang. It will basically be

00:01:43.179 --> 00:01:46.709
the story that will showcase what this new
regeneration is going to be. It will spell

00:01:46.709 --> 00:01:51.029
out his new personality and inform what his
relationship with Clara is going to be like

00:01:51.029 --> 00:01:56.869
and set up the big over-arching plot. Remember,
when Matt Smith debuted in series 5, they

00:01:56.869 --> 00:02:03.659
used that first episode to set up the Cracks
in the Universe.

00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:07.340
There will be a short cameo from Matt Smith.
It only supposed to be the audio from a phone

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:10.959
call that he placed before his regeneration.
That's what all the business with Handles

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:13.709
and the Phone was during the Christmas Special
last year.

00:02:13.709 --> 00:02:17.810
Episode 2 - This is also from Ben Wheatley,
he's doing both the first two episodes.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:21.829
The only teasers we've got are that it's
a Dalek story and The Doctor will be going

00:02:21.829 --> 00:02:28.260
"behind enemy lines" and he teased the
word Lasagna. As Daleks do not eat Lasagna

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:32.989
I have no idea what that means, but it's
possible that the Doctor could be going to

00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:38.230
Skaro again or he could be visiting a planet
in the middle of a Dalek battle.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:41.849
If you remember, at the beginning of Series
7 the Doctor traveled to Skaro but it was

00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:46.140
just a trick. So Skaro is still in ruins but
it is there. I think it was destroyed before

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:51.430
the end of the Time War. So I don't think
the events of the 50th Anniversary affected

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:52.500
it.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:57.459
Episode 3 - This is Mark Gatiss' episode
and the rumored title is Robots of Sherwood.

00:02:57.459 --> 00:03:02.469
Tom Riley is playing Robin Hood, Ben Miller
is the Sheriff of Nottingham, Trevor Cooper

00:03:02.469 --> 00:03:07.900
is Friar Tuck. It's the knights that are
the robots. Jenna Louise Coleman even gets

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.799
to shoot a bow Lord of The Rings style.

00:03:10.799 --> 00:03:15.170
Episode 4 - The title is rumored to be Listen.
This is Samuel Anderson's first episode.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:20.689
And the premise is "when you talk to yourself,
what if the person you were talking to isn't

00:03:20.689 --> 00:03:25.959
really you?" This just reminds me of Nightmare
in Silver when Mr Clever was trying to take

00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:30.489
over The Doctor's Brain and The Doctor was
talking to himself, but technically he was

00:03:30.489 --> 00:03:33.409
talking to Mr Clever who was also inside his
mind.

00:03:33.409 --> 00:03:39.989
Robert Goodman's character is only listed
as Reg, and the only other Reg I know was

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:43.719
the husband of Madge Arwell from the 2012
Christmas Special. The Doctor, The Widow and

00:03:43.719 --> 00:03:47.140
the Wardrobe. Robert Goodman looks way older
than that person, so either he's a totally

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.769
different character or he's an older version
of him.

00:03:49.769 --> 00:03:55.599
Episode 5 - The rumored title is Time Heist.
It's Keeley Hawes episode where she'll

00:03:55.599 --> 00:03:59.409
plays Ms Delphox. She supposedly works at
a bank in the far future, which would explain

00:03:59.409 --> 00:04:05.219
the heist theme. But she's also supposed
to have a dark secret. That's just the description.

00:04:05.219 --> 00:04:10.620
I know a lot of people are theorizing she
might be the Rani or even a female master.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:15.400
The funny thing about that is that almost
every single cast member except for Clara

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.350
is rumored to be the new Master.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:23.880
Episode 6 -- We don't know what the title
is, but it's supposed to take place at Coal

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:28.580
Hill School with The Doctor posing as the
Caretaker. We got to see a little bit of the

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:32.640
inside of the School when Clara was finishing
a lesson during the 50th Anniversary Special.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.640
Episode 7 -- The rumored title is Kill the
Moon. And we have seen a few set pictures

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:41.530
of Danny Pink in a spacesuit outside the TARDIS,
so I think we can connect those with this

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:41.770
episode.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:45.980
I don't want to say there's a plot to
blow up the moon, but a title like Kill the

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:50.180
Moon implies something might get destroyed.
I does also kind of make me think of The Doctor's

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:55.310
Wife with Father being a living organism inhabiting
an asteroid. So maybe there will be something

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.700
living inside the Moon that the Doctor will
have to save.

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:01.220
Episode 8 -- The rumored title is Mummy on
the Orient Express.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:06.620
Then the rumored titled of episode 9 is Flatline
and we don't know anything about episodes

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:08.250
10 through 13 yet.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:13.100
We get the best info whenever they shoot outdoor
scenes because people are able to take pictures.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:16.800
We don't know who the writers or directors
are of those last 4 episodes, but Neil Gaiman

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.630
is going to try and write another episode
depending on his schedule working out and

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:24.770
Peter Jackson said that talk of him directing
an episode was getting serious.

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:29.360
He had joked about directing an episode last
year, but because of production on The Hobbit

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:33.130
it wasn't taken too seriously. But if anything
changes I'll be sure to post an update.

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:36.080
Steven Moffat hasn't officially announced
what they're doing at Comic Con but there's

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:40.960
usually a tumblr meetup and they're pretty
good about bringing footage. So plan for either

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:45.670
the first full trailer or the first episode.
If they show a big trailer in the next month

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:48.280
I'd say the odds of them showing the whole
episode are pretty good.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.400
Now that we're getting closer to the premiere
I'll start doing more bonus videos, so be

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:49.470
sure to subscribe to get everything and be
sure to leave me suggestions for stuff you

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:49.550
guys want to talk about. Also let me know
if you guys want me to do a Doctor Who Q&amp;A

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:49.570
video this week.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:51.020
My schedule is kind of crazy right now just
because I'm out of town at a wedding and

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:51.730
I'm already behind on my Game of Thrones
bonus video. But I'll try to get everything

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:51.860
Right now click here to learn about some of
the new characters in series 8 and click here

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:51.940
for the top 10 monsters I think they should
bring back.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:52.000
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.
High Fives!

